==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[rule]] of [[law]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|legal|often|capitalized}} The [[doctrine]] that no individual is above the law and that everyone must answer to it.
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[maxim]] whereby governmental decisions are made by applying known legal principles.
# {{&lit|en|rule|law}}
#* Section 2(1), [https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/IDA1976 Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (Singapore)]
#*: In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires—{{...}} “'''rule of law'''” includes written law; {{...}}
#* Section 32(2)(b), [https://legislation.govt.nz/act/public/2019/0058/latest/DLM7298282.html Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand)]
#*: The repeal of legislation does not revive {{...}} a '''rule of law''' that has been abolished.

